Hello dveeden! I am the reporter of the issue with Connector/J :) Usually, this bug is hard to reproduce because some problems are related to the network status.

The response packets should be large enough and the PMTU should be small enough so that the responses will be divided into multiple segments. This issue will happen only when the last segment contains a part of the EOF packet or the total EOF packet.

For the test case, I guess one reason it is not working is that the destination is the loopback(127.0.0.1), in which the PMTU is set to a maximum possible value, as for my machine it is 65535.
```
> ping -s 65535 -M do 127.0.0.1  
Error: packet size 65535 is too large. Maximum is 65507
```

I also submitted a test case for this (mysql/mysql-connector-j#74) before, not sure if it can help you to reproduce the bug or not.
